{{also|Wieder|wieder-}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{cog|gmh|wider}}, whence {{cog|en|widdershins}} via {{etym|gml|-}} borrowing; from {{etyl|goh|de}} {{m|goh|widar}}, from {{inh|goh|gem-pro|*wiþer}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈviːdɐ/|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-at-wieder.ogg|audio (Austria)|lang=de}}
* {{homophones|wider|lang=de}}

===Adverb===
{{de-adv}}

# [[again]]
#: {{ux|de|Siehst du, jetzt hast du’s schon '''wieder''' gesagt!|See, now you’ve said it '''again!'''}}
# [[back]] (always with a specified destination)
#: {{ux|de|Wenn du einen Pasch würfelst, musst du '''wieder''' zum Anfangsfeld.|When you throw doublets, you must go '''back''' to the start.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|back}} {{l|de|zurück}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|de|hin und wieder}}
* {{l|de|immer wieder}}

